(1243426, 156032, 7033, '<td valign="top">I would lose the border. Very nice image. Perfect for stock.</td>', 'I would lose the border. Very nice image. Perfect for stock.', '2005-03-22 16:17:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(1243427, 158131, 7033, '<td valign="top">I can taste them. Good job.</td>', 'I can taste them. Good job.', '2005-03-22 16:17:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(1243429, 158000, 6999, '<td valign="top">I wonder if this is really close enough to serve: sure it shows location, but there is nothing specific about that location. There are strong elements I really like in it - the texture and depth of the rocks, the poses of the seals - but as successful stock: hell, I don''t know.</td>', 'I wonder if this is really close enough to serve: sure it shows location, but there is nothing specific about that location. There are strong elements I really like in it - the texture and depth of the rocks, the poses of the seals - but as successful stock: hell, I don''t know.', '2005-03-22 16:18:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(1243437, 157379, 6999, '<td valign="top">Wonderful depth of field, definition, neat composition, colour tones perfect, great light. Hate the way you''ve bordered it - really hate it, but am trying not to let it affect my vote. I think it would sell.</td>', 'Wonderful depth of field, definition, neat composition, colour tones perfect, great light. Hate the way you''ve bordered it - really hate it, but am trying not to let it affect my vote. I think it would sell.', '2005-03-22 16:21:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(1243460, 156812, 7033, '<td valign="top">A good laugh! Nice play on words.</td>', 'A good laugh! Nice play on words.', '2005-03-22 16:34:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(1243461, 156553, 7033, '<td valign="top">Wow! So jealous you got this shot. Nice job! Perfect for stock.</td>', 'Wow! So jealous you got this shot. Nice job! Perfect for stock.', '2005-03-22 16:35:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(1243484, 157870, 6999, '<td valign="top">Knockout. I don''t suppose there''s much to say about it - everything you hoped it could be, it is, I suspect. Proper grown-up, <i>modern</i> photography.</td>', 'Knockout. I don''t suppose there''s much to say about it - everything you hoped it could be, it is, I suspect. Proper grown-up, modern photography.', '2005-03-22 16:52:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(1243486, 157884, 6999, '<td valign="top">Even without the hugely overblown highlights on the child''s face and head, I''d have my doubts about the suitability of this for stock. Add the no-composition element (subject placement in frame, half a watering-can, random nature of disorganised background), and the snap-shot nature of the overall look, and I can''t see this doing anything at all here. Looks like it was shot with a high-quality camera, or at least carefully re-sized and presented though. 2</td>', 'Even without the hugely overblown highlights on the child''s face and head, I''d have my doubts about the suitability of this for stock. Add the no-composition element (subject placement in frame, half a watering-can, random nature of disorganised background), and the snap-shot nature of the overall look, and I can''t see this doing anything at all here. Looks like it was shot with a high-quality camera, or at least carefully re-sized and presented though. 2', '2005-03-22 16:55:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(1243487, 158069, 6999, '<td valign="top">So much clutter ... and dust-motes either on lens or sensor showing also.</td>', 'So much clutter ... and dust-motes either on lens or sensor showing also.', '2005-03-22 16:56:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(1243489, 158131, 6999, '<td valign="top">Basically very good - certainly pretty competent; though for this ''buyer'' you''ve over-done the fill light (kills some of the shaping of the pears), and the shadows look forced in processing - kind of unnatural, a bit sudden. The key-light is very effective however, especially on the water drops. Not an image I like very much, but then this is a stock challenge, so i didn''t expect to like the good ones really :-)</td>', 'Basically very good - certainly pretty competent; though for this ''buyer'' you''ve over-done the fill light (kills some of the shaping of the pears), and the shadows look forced in processing - kind of unnatural, a bit sudden. The key-light is very effective however, especially on the water drops. Not an image I like very much, but then this is a stock challenge, so i didn''t expect to like the good ones really :-)', '2005-03-22 16:59:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(1243492, 157444, 6999, '<td valign="top">Confusing, I think. The lemon lacks colour - it looks green, more than anything, and washed-out, muddy, and surely for stock that should be bright punchy yellow? whatever tthe container is draws far too much attention, especially as it contains the brightest highlights in the image.</td>', 'Confusing, I think. The lemon lacks colour - it looks green, more than anything, and washed-out, muddy, and surely for stock that should be bright punchy yellow? whatever tthe container is draws far too much attention, especially as it contains the brightest highlights in the image.', '2005-03-22 17:01:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(1243497, 156397, 6999, '<td valign="top">My immediate thought is that you''ve missed the opportunity for a really good composition here - those three buildings with collonades are perfectly placed relative to one another for a very striking picture - but who knows whether you had the zoom etc. to do that? This seems confused - in sense of period, composition (the gridge and bright lights way off image right - and negative space above and below - makes the sky and foreground almmost seem like a border top and bottom, but it''s just black, pretty much.</td>', 'My immediate thought is that you''ve missed the opportunity for a really good composition here - those three buildings with collonades are perfectly placed relative to one another for a very striking picture - but who knows whether you had the zoom etc. to do that? This seems confused - in sense of period, composition (the gridge and bright lights way off image right - and negative space above and below - makes the sky and foreground almmost seem like a border top and bottom, but it''s just black, pretty much.', '2005-03-22 17:04:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(1243500, 157512, 6999, '<td valign="top">Strong. The brighter background is a shame, as it pulls attention from the near-abstract qualities of the oiled/decayed metal, and what would otherwise have been a seriously powerful image. Strong sense of texture, tonality, light (other than that background, of course).</td>', 'Strong. The brighter background is a shame, as it pulls attention from the near-abstract qualities of the oiled/decayed metal, and what would otherwise have been a seriously powerful image. Strong sense of texture, tonality, light (other than that background, of course).', '2005-03-22 17:06:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(1243505, 157375, 6999, '<td valign="top">I get a sense of none of this being quite in focus - as though you''ve AF''d on the exxtreme front edge of the fallen piece, with a very shallow DOF, and so missed most of the actual subjects: the lines on the board are a give-away. I like the sense of light, however. Such images as this - fundamentally using the chess pieces to replace people as subjects -  are so very common, that I think the highest technical virtues are absolutely necessary to their success.</td>', 'I get a sense of none of this being quite in focus - as though you''ve AF''d on the exxtreme front edge of the fallen piece, with a very shallow DOF, and so missed most of the actual subjects: the lines on the board are a give-away. I like the sense of light, however. Such images as this - fundamentally using the chess pieces to replace people as subjects -  are so very common, that I think the highest technical virtues are absolutely necessary to their success.', '2005-03-22 17:10:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(1243508, 157889, 24976, '<td valign="top">it would have been better if there wasnt a shadow and semi grey gradient on the white background.</td>', 'it would have been better if there wasnt a shadow and semi grey gradient on the white background.', '2005-03-22 17:11:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(1243512, 158114, 24976, '<td valign="top">this is awesome! where i worked they dyed the cheese and eggs green so we had green omlets and green pizzas. lol, anyways really good idea and excellent execution.</td>', 'this is awesome! where i worked they dyed the cheese and eggs green so we had green omlets and green pizzas. lol, anyways really good idea and excellent execution.', '2005-03-22 17:14:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(1243513, 156840, 6999, '<td valign="top">Very pretty. i have a big issue with your placement of that wood in the foreground, and your cropping of the shaped sand around it that would really draw the eye is only you''d ncluded enough of it. Surely just crouching down would have enabled you to place that part of your composition more closely to the background, and to thus give some sense of continuity to the scene rather than this dissociation - an effect only enhanced by the very weird light around the wood. <br/> <br/>The reason that very low placemtn is a problem is one not often understood, I think: and not as simple as a ''rule of thirds'' thing, but more to do with how easily your viewer''s eye will wander out of fframe if you give it half a chance - and that placement is just the half-chance needed.</td>', 'Very pretty. i have a big issue with your placement of that wood in the foreground, and your cropping of the shaped sand around it that would really draw the eye is only you''d ncluded enough of it. Surely just crouching down would have enabled you to place that part of your composition more closely to the background, and to thus give some sense of continuity to the scene rather than this dissociation - an effect only enhanced by the very weird light around the wood.  The reason that very low placemtn is a problem is one not often understood, I think: and not as simple as a ''rule of thirds'' thing, but more to do with how easily your viewer''s eye will wander out of fframe if you give it half a chance - and that placement is just the half-chance needed.', '2005-03-22 17:14:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(1243514, 157275, 6999, '<td valign="top">Had the comment about the proper name of this thing yet?</td>', 'Had the comment about the proper name of this thing yet?', '2005-03-22 17:16:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(1243519, 158042, 6999, '<td valign="top">An interesting study, certainly. All mouse shots remind meof a shot I once missed ... ah well. My problem with this is with the lack of much cable being visible - seen from this weird angle (though effective), I think it needs something like that to really say ''MOUSE'' to the stock world. Being picky, of course. cool texxture and light, though I would perhaps have edited up the foreground to w whiter point.</td>', 'An interesting study, certainly. All mouse shots remind meof a shot I once missed ... ah well. My problem with this is with the lack of much cable being visible - seen from this weird angle (though effective), I think it needs something like that to really say ''MOUSE'' to the stock world. Being picky, of course. cool texxture and light, though I would perhaps have edited up the foreground to w whiter point.', '2005-03-22 17:25:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(1243521, 156829, 6999, '<td valign="top">I think you''ll get hit by the quality police for this one - sharpening artefacts, and blocky sense of compression. It''s a strong image though, which might allow some poorness of quality. I think you could successfully have allowed a bit more space around the main subjects however - never forget how easily the eye is lead out of your frame ...</td>', 'I think you''ll get hit by the quality police for this one - sharpening artefacts, and blocky sense of compression. It''s a strong image though, which might allow some poorness of quality. I think you could successfully have allowed a bit more space around the main subjects however - never forget how easily the eye is lead out of your frame ...', '2005-03-22 17:28:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(1243525, 157451, 6999, '<td valign="top">Nearly ideal - though i could wish for more detail brought out of the shadow side of his(?) face. Photographically, as presented, I also think you could privilege him in fame more strongly - it looks like the body angle would sit well in a composition that moved him to the right solidly - and would give the buyers somewhere for their text, also.</td>', 'Nearly ideal - though i could wish for more detail brought out of the shadow side of his(?) face. Photographically, as presented, I also think you could privilege him in fame more strongly - it looks like the body angle would sit well in a composition that moved him to the right solidly - and would give the buyers somewhere for their text, also.', '2005-03-22 17:31:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(1243527, 156747, 6999, '<td valign="top">His face, his face!</td>', 'His face, his face!', '2005-03-22 17:31:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(1243530, 157898, 6999, '<td valign="top">More tuxedo? I can imagine a composition with this button-hold placed strongly top right of frame, and showing much more of the structure of tux and waistcoat - this seems simply to be of the ''Bouttoniere''</td>', 'More tuxedo? I can imagine a composition with this button-hold placed strongly top right of frame, and showing much more of the structure of tux and waistcoat - this seems simply to be of the ''Bouttoniere''', '2005-03-22 17:33:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(1243532, 157735, 6999, '<td valign="top">I really want something to give a sense of scale to this: nothing here says anything about how damn big the angel is. Other than that, i can imagine this selling, though.</td>', 'I really want something to give a sense of scale to this: nothing here says anything about how damn big the angel is. Other than that, i can imagine this selling, though.', '2005-03-22 17:35:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(1243534, 157452, 6999, '<td valign="top">I think you''ll win, out of what i''ve seen so far. Minor gripes about verticality of tower, placing of figure, and ''storm'' in your title - it looks like a pleasant summer''s evening, colour-wise. The figure is a masterful necessity to a sense of scale in the image. Where is this? What is this? It looks like it should be a Landmark Trust property (qv if you don''t know them) - but not one that is familiar. More than anything, I think you''ll win because it''s just nearly impossible to vote this down for anything.</td>', 'I think you''ll win, out of what i''ve seen so far. Minor gripes about verticality of tower, placing of figure, and ''storm'' in your title - it looks like a pleasant summer''s evening, colour-wise. The figure is a masterful necessity to a sense of scale in the image. Where is this? What is this? It looks like it should be a Landmark Trust property (qv if you don''t know them) - but not one that is familiar. More than anything, I think you''ll win because it''s just nearly impossible to vote this down for anything.', '2005-03-22 17:38:37.000000', NULL, 1),
