(1252096, 158065, 23458, '<td valign="top">Great idea, fantastic composition. This is prototypical stock material. 9</td>', 'Great idea, fantastic composition. This is prototypical stock material. 9', '2005-03-27 07:20:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(1252110, 158065, 23478, '<td valign="top">Cute shot.</td>', 'Cute shot.', '2005-03-27 08:09:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(1252113, 158048, 4281, '<td valign="top">A logo should preferably not been seen in a stock photograph. In addition you should use a larger image size. The maximum size is 640 in either direction. Use that.<br/>As for the image I fail to see the point with it. Why are all those elements needed, the calculator, the mouse, the keyboard and the money? Of what are you taking a photograph? Remember, less is more and that very much applies to this photograph.</td>', 'A logo should preferably not been seen in a stock photograph. In addition you should use a larger image size. The maximum size is 640 in either direction. Use that.As for the image I fail to see the point with it. Why are all those elements needed, the calculator, the mouse, the keyboard and the money? Of what are you taking a photograph? Remember, less is more and that very much applies to this photograph.', '2005-03-27 08:48:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(1252114, 157072, 8891, '<td valign="top">OK image but stock wise, from what I have been seeing all about in business depictions in print and on websites, there would have been total focus on the subject and the background would be totally blurred to the point of bokeh. A vertical presentation and more height above the subect might have worked better as well, diminishing the background as it is perhaps too prominent in this. 7</td>', 'OK image but stock wise, from what I have been seeing all about in business depictions in print and on websites, there would have been total focus on the subject and the background would be totally blurred to the point of bokeh. A vertical presentation and more height above the subect might have worked better as well, diminishing the background as it is perhaps too prominent in this. 7', '2005-03-27 08:52:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(1252116, 156829, 4281, '<td valign="top">It''s a nice subject, I have to agree with that.<br/>However, the picture is oversharpened to the point that it is quite distracting.<br/>In addition I think this picture would have been improved a lot if it were in B&amp;W instead of color. As a black and white picture I would probably also say that the contrast should be increased a bit, the dark area below the clouds should especially be made darker, I think and also the blue sky to increase the contrast between the sky and the clouds.</td>', 'It''s a nice subject, I have to agree with that.However, the picture is oversharpened to the point that it is quite distracting.In addition I think this picture would have been improved a lot if it were in B&W instead of color. As a black and white picture I would probably also say that the contrast should be increased a bit, the dark area below the clouds should especially be made darker, I think and also the blue sky to increase the contrast between the sky and the clouds.', '2005-03-27 08:54:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(1252118, 157855, 31443, '<td valign="top">Love the colors but the image could have been a little clearer...the lighting from the right side is so nice, wish you had brought more of it into the basket...</td>', 'Love the colors but the image could have been a little clearer...the lighting from the right side is so nice, wish you had brought more of it into the basket...', '2005-03-27 08:56:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(1252120, 157619, 4281, '<td valign="top">For photographs like these I consider it essential to be able to see the surfer''s face -especially if one were to actually try to market it as a stock photo. <br/>I''m also not very fond of the colors in the picture, perhaps high-contrast B&amp;W would suit it better?</td>', 'For photographs like these I consider it essential to be able to see the surfer''s face -especially if one were to actually try to market it as a stock photo. I''m also not very fond of the colors in the picture, perhaps high-contrast B&W would suit it better?', '2005-03-27 08:57:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(1252121, 157584, 4281, '<td valign="top">A bit of a cliche, but then again cliches sell (and score high on dpchallenge). ;)<br/>Anyway, I would really have liked this photograph if there were more a foreground - a person standing and looking at the view would have, I think, been terrific.<br/>The sun also seems to be to your right so I think a polarizer would have been nice here to make the sky a bit bluer. (You didn''t use a polarizer, did you?)<br/>I''m also curious whether a fill flash pointed to the dark area at the top would have made the picture stronger (that is, if that area is small enough for flash to be useable).</td>', 'A bit of a cliche, but then again cliches sell (and score high on dpchallenge). ;)Anyway, I would really have liked this photograph if there were more a foreground - a person standing and looking at the view would have, I think, been terrific.The sun also seems to be to your right so I think a polarizer would have been nice here to make the sky a bit bluer. (You didn''t use a polarizer, did you?)I''m also curious whether a fill flash pointed to the dark area at the top would have made the picture stronger (that is, if that area is small enough for flash to be useable).', '2005-03-27 09:03:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(1252124, 158009, 31443, '<td valign="top">Very sweet....</td>', 'Very sweet....', '2005-03-27 09:09:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(1252125, 157887, 4281, '<td valign="top">Now, what I would probably have done differently here would to have gone much lower and tilt the camera slightly downwards to be able to use the small stream as a foreground. As it is there isn''t really much of a foreground in this picture.<br/>I''m also of the opinion that photographs with a lot of small details are less useable as dcp entries as the image size one can use is so small.</td>', 'Now, what I would probably have done differently here would to have gone much lower and tilt the camera slightly downwards to be able to use the small stream as a foreground. As it is there isn''t really much of a foreground in this picture.I''m also of the opinion that photographs with a lot of small details are less useable as dcp entries as the image size one can use is so small.', '2005-03-27 09:09:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(1252127, 157947, 4281, '<td valign="top">The sepia effect here is much too strong. In addition this is one those cases where the addition of a person in the photograph actually makes the picture worse as the man controlling the train is much too modern looking (lose the sunglasses, please) and in addition looking downwards instead of in the camera or at the rail-track.<br/>I also fail to see the point with including the sky in the picture as it is totally white and of no interest.</td>', 'The sepia effect here is much too strong. In addition this is one those cases where the addition of a person in the photograph actually makes the picture worse as the man controlling the train is much too modern looking (lose the sunglasses, please) and in addition looking downwards instead of in the camera or at the rail-track.I also fail to see the point with including the sky in the picture as it is totally white and of no interest.', '2005-03-27 09:13:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(1252129, 158071, 4281, '<td valign="top">Look at the other glasses with a book photograph in this challenge and notice why it is superior to you your entry. <br/>a) If a short portion of text could have been seen through the glasses the picture would have been better.<br/>b) Cutting the glasses in half as you have done with your crop is quite distracting.</td>', 'Look at the other glasses with a book photograph in this challenge and notice why it is superior to you your entry. a) If a short portion of text could have been seen through the glasses the picture would have been better.b) Cutting the glasses in half as you have done with your crop is quite distracting.', '2005-03-27 09:18:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(1252130, 157737, 31443, '<td valign="top">Looks like Spring isn''t far off, very nice contrasts</td>', 'Looks like Spring isn''t far off, very nice contrasts', '2005-03-27 09:19:59.000000', NULL, 1),
