(1255385, 156635, 31637, '<td valign="top">Thank you guys for taking time to comment. This is a favorite spot of mine right down the block from the World Trade Ctr. I did not know what to expect with this, I am very happy with it''s placing. Your comments mean a lot!</td>', 'Thank you guys for taking time to comment. This is a favorite spot of mine right down the block from the World Trade Ctr. I did not know what to expect with this, I am very happy with it''s placing. Your comments mean a lot!', '2005-03-28 22:26:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(1255398, 157584, 7033, '<td valign="top">Thanks all for the comments... and the ribbon!  I almost second-guessed my wife on this one, but as I mentioned in the main description, she often has better tastes than I do.  There were so many other great shots in this challenge I figured I would be doing well to get a top-ten finish.<br/> <br/>I would love to have had a better camera to have perhaps done this shot a bit differently.  My camera is a simple point-and-shoot model, all but eliminating the possibility of using a polarizer or for the on-board flash to fill such a large space (as noted by some in their comments).  And the 4mp resolution is barely enough to get a decent-sized print done-- my next task.<br/> <br/>Ideal conditions, including the cloud-filled sky and a stiff northerly breeze keeping the haze out of the way are probably more responsible for the quality of the shot than anything at my own hands.<br/> <br/>Again, my thanks for your comments!</td>', 'Thanks all for the comments... and the ribbon!  I almost second-guessed my wife on this one, but as I mentioned in the main description, she often has better tastes than I do.  There were so many other great shots in this challenge I figured I would be doing well to get a top-ten finish. I would love to have had a better camera to have perhaps done this shot a bit differently.  My camera is a simple point-and-shoot model, all but eliminating the possibility of using a polarizer or for the on-board flash to fill such a large space (as noted by some in their comments).  And the 4mp resolution is barely enough to get a decent-sized print done-- my next task. Ideal conditions, including the cloud-filled sky and a stiff northerly breeze keeping the haze out of the way are probably more responsible for the quality of the shot than anything at my own hands. Again, my thanks for your comments!', '2005-03-28 22:33:14.000000', NULL, 0),
