(1257061, 156635, 8860, '<td valign="top"><b>:: Hello from the Critique Club ::</b> <br/>............................................................<br/> <br/>Well Tony, while I didn''t vote or comment on this challenge, I have to say that your shot stood out a mile as a thumbnail - and it''s no disappointment when viewed at full size.<br/> <br/>This all goes without saying really but your photo is dynamic in its composition, colours and choice of focus. You''ve got some amazing lighting and you''ve processed it very well indeed. As a piece of stock photography it fits well enough for the a niche purpose, so no probs there either.<br/> <br/>All in all, it''s a great exposure, a strong, graphical subject and neat piece of memorable photography.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/>Jon</td>', ':: Hello from the Critique Club :: ............................................................ Well Tony, while I didn''t vote or comment on this challenge, I have to say that your shot stood out a mile as a thumbnail - and it''s no disappointment when viewed at full size. This all goes without saying really but your photo is dynamic in its composition, colours and choice of focus. You''ve got some amazing lighting and you''ve processed it very well indeed. As a piece of stock photography it fits well enough for the a niche purpose, so no probs there either. All in all, it''s a great exposure, a strong, graphical subject and neat piece of memorable photography. CheersJon', '2005-03-29 20:16:42.000000', NULL, 0),
