(1257471, 158075, 33079, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by larushka:</b></div><hr/><i> My daughter goes to school opposite this place (UCSD) I have taken some great shots of the hanggliders but nothing like this!  Seems like this a hangout for Rebel/300D users!  I''m especially glad to note that you used the kit lens for this picture - there is so much controversy over this lens'' capabilities - I keep thinking I need to spend more money on L lenses, but this winning picture has changed my mind... </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I also keep thinking about buying a better lens. The optics in the kit lens seems to be good enough for my level, but due to shaky mechanics the lens does not appear to me as a precise optical device.  I do not think my picture will do a right thing if it prevents you from getting the lens of your dream.<br/> <br/>Thanks again for the great comments to all of you,  Nikolai<br/> <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by larushka: My daughter goes to school opposite this place (UCSD) I have taken some great shots of the hanggliders but nothing like this!  Seems like this a hangout for Rebel/300D users!  I''m especially glad to note that you used the kit lens for this picture - there is so much controversy over this lens'' capabilities - I keep thinking I need to spend more money on L lenses, but this winning picture has changed my mind...   I also keep thinking about buying a better lens. The optics in the kit lens seems to be good enough for my level, but due to shaky mechanics the lens does not appear to me as a precise optical device.  I do not think my picture will do a right thing if it prevents you from getting the lens of your dream. Thanks again for the great comments to all of you,  Nikolai ', '2005-03-30 00:00:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(1257840, 156635, 32285, '<td valign="top">Very cool shot! I like the colors and the lights!</td>', 'Very cool shot! I like the colors and the lights!', '2005-03-30 01:54:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(1258036, 156437, 31637, '<td valign="top">Greetings from CC.<br/> <br/>The GOOD:  Excellent selective focus. It''s a very crisp shot.  I like your use of lighting, perfect exposure. I like the off center composition and DOF is great, very shallow. Cropped perfectly no noise considering High ISO.<br/> <br/>The Bad:  Not a big fan of selective focus on animals, thats just my opinion though. <br/> <br/>The Ugly: nothing here...great use of shutter <br/></td>', 'Greetings from CC. The GOOD:  Excellent selective focus. It''s a very crisp shot.  I like your use of lighting, perfect exposure. I like the off center composition and DOF is great, very shallow. Cropped perfectly no noise considering High ISO. The Bad:  Not a big fan of selective focus on animals, thats just my opinion though.  The Ugly: nothing here...great use of shutter ', '2005-03-30 02:50:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(1258290, 157975, 28801, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club<br/> <br/>The first thing that strikes me about this photo is the gentle simplicity of it. The soft pastel-like colours give it a texture you can almost feel.  The shadow underneath enhances the appearance of depth. The white background is most appropriate for the subject matter. The green border is a nice touch that matches the stem of the flower. All in all an excellent composition and I cant find anything I would change about it.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club The first thing that strikes me about this photo is the gentle simplicity of it. The soft pastel-like colours give it a texture you can almost feel.  The shadow underneath enhances the appearance of depth. The white background is most appropriate for the subject matter. The green border is a nice touch that matches the stem of the flower. All in all an excellent composition and I cant find anything I would change about it.', '2005-03-30 06:46:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(1258611, 158132, 32498, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>Hello,<br/>I think your overall composition and placement of the main subject is good although moving it to the left a bit would have improved it alittle.  The road coming in from the right doesnt bother me and tends to keep my eye focused on the bucket and tree as your main subject.  I think muting the background or a better use of selective focus would have helped in allowing the subject to stand out more from the background.  My eye does tend to wander to the left at the bright snow and darker background tree.  The overall mood of the picture helps support your subject.  If it had been a bright sunny day there would have just been too many distractions and conflicts.  Not a bad shot but I think working on separating your subject more from the background would have really helped.</td>', '*Critique Club* Hello,I think your overall composition and placement of the main subject is good although moving it to the left a bit would have improved it alittle.  The road coming in from the right doesnt bother me and tends to keep my eye focused on the bucket and tree as your main subject.  I think muting the background or a better use of selective focus would have helped in allowing the subject to stand out more from the background.  My eye does tend to wander to the left at the bright snow and darker background tree.  The overall mood of the picture helps support your subject.  If it had been a bright sunny day there would have just been too many distractions and conflicts.  Not a bad shot but I think working on separating your subject more from the background would have really helped.', '2005-03-30 10:49:15.000000', NULL, 0),
